#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits are executed on IBM&reg; hardware as sequences of microwave pulses that need to be scheduled and run at precise time intervals.\n"
"Unfortunately, unwanted interactions between qubits can lead to coherent errors on idling qubits. Dynamical decoupling works by inserting pulse sequences on idling qubits to approximately cancel out the effect of these errors. Each inserted pulse sequence amounts to an identity operation, but the physical presence of the pulses has the effect of suppressing errors.\n"
"There are many possible choices of pulse sequences, and which sequence is better for each particular case remains an [active area of research](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga quantum circuit ay isinasagawa sa IBM&reg; hardware bilang mga sequence ng microwave pulse na kailangang i-schedule at patakbuhin sa tiyak na mga agwat ng oras.\n"
"Sa kasamaang palad, ang mga hindi gustong interaksyon sa pagitan ng mga qubit ay maaaring humantong sa mga coherent error sa mga idling qubit. Gumagana ang dynamical decoupling sa pamamagitan ng paglalagay ng mga pulse sequence sa mga idling qubit upang halos kanselahin ang epekto ng mga error na ito. Ang bawat na-insert na pulse sequence ay katumbas ng isang identity operation, ngunit ang pisikal na presensya ng mga pulse ay may epekto ng pag-suppress ng mga error.\n"
"Maraming posibleng pagpipilian ng mga pulse sequence, at kung aling sequence ang mas mabuti para sa bawat partikular na kaso ay nananatiling isang [aktibong larangan ng pananaliksik](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that dynamical decoupling is mainly useful for circuits containing gaps in which some qubits sit idle without any operations acting on them. If the operations in the circuit are packed very densely, such that all of the qubits are busy most of the time, then the addition of dynamical decoupling pulses might not improve performance. In fact, it could even worsen performance due to imperfections in the pulses themselves.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang dynamical decoupling ay pangunahing kapaki-pakinabang para sa mga circuit na naglalaman ng mga puwang kung saan ang ilang qubit ay idle nang walang anumang operasyon na kumikilos sa kanila. Kung ang mga operasyon sa circuit ay napakadense, kung kaya't ang lahat ng qubit ay abala karamihan sa oras, ang pagdaragdag ng mga dynamical decoupling pulse ay maaaring hindi mapabuti ang performance. Sa katunayan, maaari pa nitong mapasama ang performance dahil sa mga kakulangan ng mismong mga pulse.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagram below depicts dynamical decoupling with an XX pulse sequence. The abstract circuit on the left is mapped onto a microwave pulse schedule on the top right. The bottom right depicts the same schedule, but with a sequence of two X pulses inserted during an idle period of the first qubit.\n"
msgstr "Ang diagram sa ibaba ay naglalarawan ng dynamical decoupling gamit ang isang XX pulse sequence. Ang abstract circuit sa kaliwa ay nima-map sa isang microwave pulse schedule sa kanang tuktok. Ang kanang ibaba ay naglalarawan ng parehong schedule, ngunit may isang sequence ng dalawang X pulse na ipinasok sa panahon ng idle period ng unang qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Depiction of dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable dynamical decoupling the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Dynamical decoupling transpiler pass](/guides/dynamical-decoupling-pass-manager) in Qiskit\n"
"    - The dynamical decoupling option if using IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#dynamical_decoupling) or [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#dynamical_decoupling)\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong i-enable ang dynamical decoupling sa mga sumusunod na paraan:\n"
"    - Ang [Dynamical decoupling transpiler pass](/guides/dynamical-decoupling-pass-manager) sa Qiskit\n"
"    - Ang dynamical decoupling option kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#dynamical_decoupling) o [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#dynamical_decoupling)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirling, also known as [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), is a widely used technique for converting arbitrary noise channels into noise channels with more specific structure.\n"
msgstr "Ang twirling, na kilala rin bilang [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), ay isang malawakang ginagamit na teknik para sa pag-convert ng mga arbitrary na noise channel sa mga noise channel na may mas tiyak na istraktura.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is a special kind of twirling that uses Pauli operations. It has the effect of transforming any quantum channel into a Pauli channel. Performed alone, it can mitigate coherent noise because coherent noise tends to accumulate quadratically with the number of operations, whereas Pauli noise accumulates linearly. Pauli twirling is often combined with other error mitigation techniques that work better with Pauli noise than with arbitrary noise.\n"
msgstr "Ang Pauli twirling ay isang espesyal na uri ng twirling na gumagamit ng mga Pauli operation. Mayroon itong epekto ng pag-transform ng anumang quantum channel sa isang Pauli channel. Kapag ginawa nang mag-isa, maaari nitong mapagaan ang coherent noise dahil ang coherent noise ay may tendency na mag-accumulate nang quadratically kasabay ng bilang ng mga operasyon, samantalang ang Pauli noise ay nag-a-accumulate nang linearly. Ang Pauli twirling ay madalas na pinagsama sa iba pang mga teknik ng error mitigation na mas gumagana sa Pauli noise kaysa sa arbitrary na noise.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is implemented by sandwiching a chosen set of gates with randomly chosen single-qubit Pauli gates in such a way that the ideal effect of the gate remains the same. The result is that a single circuit is replaced with a random ensemble of circuits, all with the same ideal effect. When sampling the circuit, samples are drawn from multiple random instances, rather than just a single one.\n"
msgstr "Ang Pauli twirling ay isinasagawa sa pamamagitan ng pag-sandwich ng isang piniling hanay ng mga gate gamit ang mga random na piniling single-qubit Pauli gate sa paraang nananatiling pareho ang ideal na epekto ng gate. Ang resulta ay ang isang circuit ay pinapalitan ng isang random na ensemble ng mga circuit, lahat ay may parehong ideal na epekto. Kapag nagsa-sample ng circuit, ang mga sample ay kinukuha mula sa maraming random na instance, hindi lang sa iisa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Depiction of Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since most of the errors in current quantum hardware come from two-qubit gates, this technique is often applied exclusively to (native) two-qubit gates. The following diagram depicts some Pauli twirls for the CNOT and ECR gates. Every circuit within a row has the same ideal effect.\n"
msgstr "Dahil karamihan sa mga error sa kasalukuyang quantum hardware ay nagmumula sa mga two-qubit gate, ang teknik na ito ay madalas na inilalapat nang eksklusibo sa mga (native) two-qubit gate. Ang sumusunod na diagram ay naglalarawan ng ilang Pauli twirl para sa mga CNOT at ECR gate. Ang bawat circuit sa loob ng isang hilera ay may parehong ideal na epekto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of gate twirls](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Depiction of gate twirls](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable Pauli twirling the following ways:\n"
"    - A [Pauli twirling custom pass](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) in Qiskit\n"
"    - The twirling options if using IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#twirling) or [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#twirling)\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong i-enable ang Pauli twirling sa mga sumusunod na paraan:\n"
"    - Isang [Pauli twirling custom pass](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) sa Qiskit\n"
"    - Ang mga twirling option kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#twirling) o [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#twirling)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"
msgstr "Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) mitigates the effect of measurement errors for the estimation of Pauli observable expectation values.\n"
"It is based on the notion of twirled measurements, which are accomplished by randomly substituting measurement gates by a sequence of (1) a Pauli X gate, (2) a measurement, and (3) classical bit flip. Just like in standard gate twirling, this sequence is equivalent to a plain measurement in the absence of noise, as depicted in the following diagram:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) ay nagpapagaan ng epekto ng mga measurement error para sa pagtatantya ng mga expectation value ng Pauli observable.\n"
"Batay ito sa konsepto ng twirled measurements, na naaabot sa pamamagitan ng random na pagpapalit ng mga measurement gate ng isang sequence ng (1) isang Pauli X gate, (2) isang measurement, at (3) classical bit flip. Tulad ng sa standard gate twirling, ang sequence na ito ay katumbas ng isang simpleng measurement kung walang noise, tulad ng inilalarawan sa sumusunod na diagram:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Depiction of measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the presence of readout error, measurement twirling has the effect of diagonalizing the readout-error transfer matrix, making it easy to invert. A rescaling term from the diagonal noise channel is learned by\n"
"benchmarking random circuits initialized in the zero state. This allows\n"
"the service to remove bias from expectation values that result from\n"
"readout noise. Estimating the readout-error transfer matrix requires executing additional calibration circuits, which introduces a small overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa presensya ng readout error, ang measurement twirling ay may epekto ng pag-diagonalize ng readout-error transfer matrix, na ginagawa itong madaling i-invert. Natututunan ang isang rescaling term mula sa diagonal noise channel sa pamamagitan ng\n"
"benchmarking ng mga random na circuit na na-initialize sa zero state. Pinapayagan nito ang\n"
"serbisyo na alisin ang bias mula sa mga expectation value na nagmumula sa\n"
"readout noise. Ang pagtatantya ng readout-error transfer matrix ay nangangailangan ng pagpapatupad ng karagdagang mga calibration circuit, na nagdudulot ng maliit na overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable TREX the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`measure_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#measure_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - The [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong i-enable ang TREX sa mga sumusunod na paraan:\n"
"    - Ang [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon para sa Qiskit\n"
"    - Ang [`measure_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#measure_mitigation) kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - Ang [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"
msgstr "Extrapolation ng zero-noise (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating errors in estimating expectation values of observables. While it often improves results, it is not guaranteed to produce an unbiased result.\n"
msgstr "Ang Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) ay isang teknik para mapagaan ang mga error sa pagtatantya ng mga expectation value ng mga observable. Habang madalas nitong pinapabuti ang mga resulta, hindi garantisado na makakagawa ito ng walang bias na resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE consists of two stages:\n"
msgstr "Ang ZNE ay binubuo ng dalawang yugto:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple times at different noise rates. (This can be done with either gate folding or [probabilistic error amplification](#pea).)\n"
msgstr "_Noise amplification_: Ang orihinal na quantum circuit ay isinasagawa nang maraming beses sa iba't ibang antas ng noise. (Magagawa ito gamit ang gate folding o [probabilistic error amplification](#pea).)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy expectation value results to the zero-noise limit. (Typically with either an exponential or polynomial.)\n"
msgstr "_Extrapolation_: Ang ideal na resulta ay tinatantya sa pamamagitan ng pag-extrapolate ng mga maingay na resulta ng expectation value patungo sa zero-noise limit. (Karaniwan gamit ang exponential o polynomial.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can be implemented in many different ways. By default, IBM Quantum Compute implements noise amplification by \"digital gate folding,\" which means that two-qubit gates are replaced with equivalent sequences of the gate and its inverse. For example, replacing a unitary $U$ with $U U^\\dagger U$ would yield a noise amplification factor of 3. For the extrapolation, you can choose from one of several functional forms, including a linear fit or an exponential fit.\n"
"The image below depicts digital gate folding on the left, and the extrapolation procedure on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang parehong noise amplification at extrapolation na yugto ay maaaring ipatupad sa maraming iba't ibang paraan. Bilang default, ang IBM Quantum Compute ay nagpapatupad ng noise amplification sa pamamagitan ng \"digital gate folding,\" na nangangahulugang ang mga two-qubit gate ay pinapalitan ng mga katumbas na sequence ng gate at ang inverse nito. Halimbawa, ang pagpapalit ng isang unitary $U$ ng $U U^\\dagger U$ ay magbubunga ng noise amplification factor na 3. Para sa extrapolation, maaari kang pumili mula sa isa sa ilang functional form, kasama ang linear fit o exponential fit.\n"
"Ang larawan sa ibaba ay naglalarawan ng digital gate folding sa kaliwa, at ang extrapolation procedure sa kanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Depiction of ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The overhead of this method scales with the number of noise factors. The\n"
"default settings sample the expectation value at three noise factors,\n"
"leading to a roughly 3x overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang overhead ng pamamaraang ito ay nag-e-scale kasabay ng bilang ng mga noise factor. Ang\n"
"mga default na setting ay nagsa-sample ng expectation value sa tatlong noise factor,\n"
"na humahantong sa halos 3x na overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable ZNE the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - The [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong i-enable ang ZNE sa mga sumusunod na paraan:\n"
"    - Ang [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon para sa Qiskit\n"
"    - Ang [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - Ang [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pea\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pea\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE with Probabilistic Error Amplification (PEA) {#zne-with-probabilistic-error-amplification-pea}"
msgstr "ZNE na may Probabilistic Error Amplification (PEA) {#zne-with-probabilistic-error-amplification-pea}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the main challenges in ZNE is to accurately amplify the noise affecting the target circuit. Gate folding provides an easy way to perform this amplification, but is potentially inaccurate and might lead to incorrect results.  See the article [\"Scalable error mitigation for noisy quantum circuits produces competitive expectation values\"](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2108.09197), and specifically page 4 of the supplementary information for details. Probabilistic error amplification provides a more accurate approach to error amplification through noise learning.\n"
msgstr "Isa sa mga pangunahing hamon sa ZNE ay ang tumpak na pag-amplify ng noise na nakakaapekto sa target na circuit. Ang gate folding ay nagbibigay ng madaling paraan para maisagawa ang amplification na ito, ngunit maaaring hindi tumpak at maaaring humantong sa maling mga resulta. Tingnan ang artikulo [\"Scalable error mitigation for noisy quantum circuits produces competitive expectation values\"](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2108.09197), at partikular ang pahina 4 ng supplementary information para sa mga detalye. Ang probabilistic error amplification ay nagbibigay ng mas tumpak na diskarte sa error amplification sa pamamagitan ng noise learning.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA is a more sophisticated technique that performs preliminary experiments to reconstruct the noise and then uses this information to perform an accurate amplification. It starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit before they are run. After the learning phase, the circuits are executed at each noise factor, where every entangling layer of the circuits is amplified by probabilistically injecting single-qubit noise proportional to the corresponding learned noise model. See the article [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3) for more details.\n"
msgstr "Ang PEA ay isang mas sopistikadong teknik na nagsasagawa ng mga paunang eksperimento upang muling itayo ang noise at pagkatapos ay ginagamit ang impormasyong ito upang maisagawa ang isang tumpak na amplification. Nagsisimula ito sa pag-aaral ng twirled noise model ng bawat layer ng mga entangling gate sa circuit bago sila patakbuhin. Pagkatapos ng learning phase, ang mga circuit ay isinasagawa sa bawat noise factor, kung saan ang bawat entangling layer ng mga circuit ay pine-amplify sa pamamagitan ng probabilistic na pag-inject ng single-qubit noise na proporsyonal sa kaukulang natutunan na noise model. Tingnan ang artikulo [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3) para sa karagdagang detalye.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEA consists of three stages:\n"
"1. _Learning_: The twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit is learned.\n"
"1. _Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple times at different noise factors.\n"
"2. _Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy expectation value results to the zero-noise limit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang PEA ay binubuo ng tatlong yugto:\n"
"1. _Learning_: Natututunan ang twirled noise model ng bawat layer ng mga entangling gate sa circuit.\n"
"1. _Noise amplification_: Ang orihinal na quantum circuit ay isinasagawa nang maraming beses sa iba't ibang noise factor.\n"
"2. _Extrapolation_: Ang ideal na resulta ay tinatantya sa pamamagitan ng pag-extrapolate ng mga maingay na resulta ng expectation value patungo sa zero-noise limit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For utility-scale experiments, PEA is often the best choice.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga eksperimento sa utility-scale, ang PEA ay madalas na pinakamainam na pagpipilian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because PEA is a ZNE noise amplification technique, you also need to enable ZNE. You can enable PEA and ZNE  the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) with [`pea`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-zne-options#amplifier) as the amplifier if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang PEA ay isang teknik ng noise amplification para sa ZNE, kailangan mo ring i-enable ang ZNE. Maaari mong i-enable ang PEA at ZNE sa mga sumusunod na paraan:\n"
"    - Ang [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon para sa Qiskit\n"
"    - Ang [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) na may [`pea`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-zne-options#amplifier) bilang amplifier kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Noise learning required\">\n"
"If you are using the new client-side Estimator introduced in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, a separate noise-learning job is required to use PEA.\n"
"See [Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for more information.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Kinakailangan ang noise learning\">\n"
"Kung ginagamit mo ang bagong client-side Estimator na ipinakilala sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, kailangan ng hiwalay na noise-learning job para magamit ang PEA.\n"
"Tingnan ang [Mag-migrate mula sa server-side patungo sa client-side na Sampler at Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pec\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pec\"></span>\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"
msgstr "Probabilistic na pagkansela ng error (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) is a technique for mitigating errors in estimating expectation values of observables. Unlike ZNE, it returns an unbiased estimate of the expectation value. However, it generally incurs a greater overhead.\n"
msgstr "Ang Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) ay isang teknik para mapagaan ang mga error sa pagtatantya ng mga expectation value ng mga observable. Hindi tulad ng ZNE, nagbabalik ito ng walang bias na tantya ng expectation value. Gayunpaman, sa pangkalahatan ito ay nagdudulot ng mas malaking overhead.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In PEC, the effect of an ideal target circuit is expressed as a linear combination of noisy circuits that are actually implementable in practice:\n"
msgstr "Sa PEC, ang epekto ng isang ideal na target circuit ay ipinahayag bilang isang linear combination ng mga maingay na circuit na aktwal na maisasagawa sa practice:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{O}_{\\text{ideal}} = \\sum_{i} \\eta_i \\mathcal{O}_{noisy, i}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{O}_{\\text{ideal}} = \\sum_{i} \\eta_i \\mathcal{O}_{noisy, i}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The output of the ideal circuit can then be reproduced by executing different noisy circuit instances drawn from a random ensemble defined by the linear combination. If the coefficients $\\eta_i$ form a probability distribution, they can be used directly as the probabilities of the ensemble. In practice, some of the coefficients are negative, so they form a quasi-probability distribution instead. They can still be used to define a random ensemble, but there is a sampling overhead related to the negativity of the quasi-probability distribution, which is characterized by the quantity\n"
msgstr "Ang output ng ideal na circuit ay maaaring muling gawin sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatupad ng iba't ibang maingay na circuit instance na kinuha mula sa isang random na ensemble na tinukoy ng linear combination. Kung ang mga coefficient na $\\eta_i$ ay bumubuo ng isang probability distribution, maaari itong gamitin nang direkta bilang mga probabilidad ng ensemble. Sa practice, ang ilan sa mga coefficient ay negatibo, kaya bumubuo sila ng isang quasi-probability distribution sa halip. Maaari pa rin itong gamitin upang tukuyin ang isang random na ensemble, ngunit may sampling overhead na kaugnay sa negativity ng quasi-probability distribution, na nailalarawan ng dami\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\gamma = \\sum_{i} \\lvert \\eta_i \\rvert \\geq 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\gamma = \\sum_{i} \\lvert \\eta_i \\rvert \\geq 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sampling overhead is a multiplicative factor on the number of shots required to estimate an expectation value to a given precision, compared to the number of shots that would be needed from the ideal circuit. It scales quadratically with $\\gamma$, which in turn scales exponentially with the depth of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang sampling overhead ay isang multiplicative factor sa bilang ng mga shot na kinakailangan upang matantya ang isang expectation value sa isang partikular na katumpakan, kumpara sa bilang ng mga shot na kakailanganin mula sa ideal na circuit. Nag-e-scale ito nang quadratically kasabay ng $\\gamma$, na nag-e-scale naman nang exponentially kasabay ng depth ng circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable PEC  the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`pec_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#pec_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong i-enable ang PEC sa mga sumusunod na paraan:\n"
"    - Ang [Qiskit Mitigation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon para sa Qiskit\n"
"    - Ang [`pec_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#pec_mitigation) kung gumagamit ng IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Noise learning required\">\n"
"If you are using the new client-side Estimator introduced in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, a separate noise-learning job is required to use PEC.\n"
"See [Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for more information.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Kinakailangan ang noise learning\">\n"
"Kung ginagamit mo ang bagong client-side Estimator na ipinakilala sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, kailangan ng hiwalay na noise-learning job para magamit ang PEC.\n"
"Tingnan ang [Mag-migrate mula sa server-side patungo sa client-side na Sampler at Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

